      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @spinler@us.ibm.com,\n\n#### Thanks for calling this out — I think the code is likely unnecessary here(and below).\n\n#### Here’s why I think this may not be needed:\n#### 1) Scope of the flag\n`isButtonMultiActionSupport` is used to decide whether we register multiple Power1~N “Released” signals. That mixes policy with topology. The flag should influence how power actions are handled, not whether we register multiple matches.\n\n#### 2) Brittleness. \nThe scan over gpio_definitions is fragile: the absence of a multi-action field in even one entry triggers `else { isButtonMultiActionSupport \u003d false; break; }`, forcing the flag to false. This is not robust and can cause under-detection of multi-button setups.\n\n#### Here are some journal log records(currrent mechanism not incude this gerrit change):\n```\u003d\nOct 26 23:52:56 bmc systemd[1]: Started Phosphor Button Handler.\nOct 26 23:52:56 bmc button-handler[6994]: [Liora] hostSelectButtonMode \u003d True\nOct 26 23:52:56 bmc button-handler[6994]: [Liora] isButtonMultiActionSupport: True (default)\nOct 26 23:52:56 bmc button-handler[6994]: [Liora] gpioConfig: {\"direction\":\"both\",\"multi-action\":[...],\"name\":\"POWER_BUTTON1\",\"pin\":\"Q0\"}\n...\nOct 26 23:52:56 bmc button-handler[6994]: [Liora] gpioConfig: {...\"name\":\"HOST_SELECTOR\",\"polling_interval_ms\":2000,\"polling_mode\":true}\nOct 26 23:52:56 bmc button-handler[6994]: [Liora]Set isButtonMultiActionSupport flag to  False\n\n```\n\n#### Regarding the above: I’ve removed isButtonMultiActionSupport since the current implementation doesn’t consume it.\n\n#### Would you prefer that we keep it? If needed, I can leave it declared in the .hpp as a policy knob for potential future use.",
